---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import { release } from '../lib/site';
---

<Site
  title="Roadmap · memprove"
  description="What memprove does today, its open limits, and what comes next on memprove.dev."
  current="roadmap"
>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="cap">[ roadmap ]</p>
        <h1 class="h2">Where memprove is, and what comes next.</h1>

        <h2>Now: {release.version}</h2>
        <p>
          The daemon and the CLI, the session-start hook for Claude Code, Codex and Cursor, the MCP server with ten tools,
          <code>memprove init</code> for Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and TRAE, the unattended takeover rule and its evaluation, and
          <code>memprove eval</code>, which runs a coding agent on the repository's own tasks and measures whether memprove's memory
          helps it. New in 0.3.0: <code>memprove verify</code> checks that work an agent says is done is done,
          <code>memprove policy</code> gives the three clients one set of tool rules, with a scan for secrets,
          <code>memprove report</code> shows what one session cost and did, and <code>memprove import</code> reads the instruction
          files a repository already has. The ledger format, the control API and the Pack's line set are stable.
          <a href="/changelog/">The changelog</a> has the details.
        </p>

        <h2>Open limits</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Release binaries cover macOS on Apple silicon and Linux x86_64. Linux on arm64 fails in the daemon's file-system sandbox; other platforms build from source.</li>
          <li>Test case counts are read from cargo and pytest output. Other runners pass <code>--test --test-cases &lt;N&gt;</code>.</li>
          <li>The repository state covers tracked files, the index, HEAD and the branch. Ignored files and environment variables are not part of it.</li>
          <li>The macOS binaries are not notarized.</li>
          <li>The hooks are tested against each client's documented hook input. In a real client, only the policy hook in Codex has been run; the session-start hooks in Codex and Cursor, Cursor's policy hook and everything for TRAE have not.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Next on memprove.dev</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>A comparison page: how other memory tools decide whether a memory still holds.</li>
          <li>The takeover evaluation's scenarios and results as a page of their own.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Follow along</h2>
        <p>
          Work is planned and discussed in the open on <a href="https://github.com/memprove/memprove/issues">GitHub issues</a>.
          Each release is announced on <a href="https://github.com/memprove/memprove/releases">GitHub Releases</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>
